Bugfix: Make implicitly nullable parameters explicit for PHP 8.4

PHP 8.4 deprecates implicitly nullable parameter types (`Type $x = null`).
ownCloud compiles such a declaration in OC\DB\Connection while it is being
loaded as the DBAL wrapper class; the deprecation is routed to the error
handler, logging needs the database connection, and DBAL then rejects the
half-loaded class with "The given 'wrapperClass' OC\DB\Connection has to be a
subtype of \Doctrine\DBAL\Connection". On PHP 8.4 an instance installs but
every occ command and web request afterwards fails.

All implicitly nullable parameters are now explicit (`?Type $x = null`, or
`A|B|null` for union types). Optional parameters that precede a required one
keep their position but lose the `= null` default, which PHP already treated
as required, so existing call sites are unaffected.

https://github.com/owncloud/core/pull/41893
